Understanding Pharmaceutical Grade Fish Oil
Pharmaceutical grade fish oil represents the highest purity tier of marine-derived omega-3 products, containing concentrated levels of eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) and docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) that meet pharmacopoeia standards. Through advanced molecular distillation and purification processes, manufacturers remove environmental contaminants while preserving bioactive compounds, making it suitable for:
1.	Prescription medications for triglyceride management
2.	Enteral and parenteral clinical nutrition formulations
3.	High-potency nutraceutical products
Unlike standard fish oil supplements, pharmaceutical-grade variants undergo rigorous testing for oxidation levels, heavy metals, and persistent organic pollutants - critical quality parameters for medical applications where safety and efficacy cannot be compromised.
